  "feedbacks": [],
  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 55 actions, all registered in one setActionDefinitions call in initActions() (index.js:737-1962). The module registers no feedbacks (no setFeedbackDefinitions call anywhere); the presets in presets.js contain feedback entries without a feedbackId, which do not refer to a registered feedback.",
    "Protocol: plain HTTP on port 80 of the processor. State is polled with GET http://<ip>:80/api/ every 1000 ms (pollIntervalMs, index.js:10); every action sets a property with GET http://<ip>:80/<api path>?set=<value> (setProcessorProperty, index.js:705). The API paths are in apiKeys.js. Config fields: ip (Regex.IP, default 192.168.0.50) and maxBrightness (default 1550, used for percentage variables).",
    "Toggle actions (*Toggle, option mode: toggle/enable/disable): enable and disable send true/false; toggle reads the current state from the last poll and fails with a log error when the state is not available.",
    "Number options set no asInteger, but the callbacks of the actions that use validate() (index.js:76-88) reject non-whole numbers at runtime: preset, frame store, brightness, colour temperature, group, group brightness and all LUT strength actions (lutStrengthSelect has step 0.1 in the UI, yet setValidatedProperty calls validate(), so a fractional strength is rejected). The phase offset, ShutterSync angle/speed/time selects use validateFloat() and accept fractions.",
    "Source quirks recorded unchanged: frameStoreFrameSelect writes to apiKeys.testPatternType (index.js:1098) instead of a frame-store key, so it is likely a copy-paste slip in the module; lutStrengthDecrease has min 0.0 while lutStrengthIncrease has min 0.1; the tooltip of lutToggle says \"14-Way Colour Correct toggle mode\"; hiddenMarkersToggle sends the lower-cased marker type (starTracker becomes startracker, redSpy becomes redspy) to api/output/network/hidden-markers/mode only when the variable hiddenMarkersMode is not \"?\".",
    "Increase/decrease actions (lutStrength*, outputBrightness*, outputColourTemperature*, groupBrightness*) read the current value from the polled state, add or subtract the step and clamp to the range; phaseOffsetIncrease/Decrease use the current phaseOffsetMode variable to choose between the angle and the fraction option and ignore the other. Group brightness uses the path api/groups/items/<group>/brightness; the group number max is Math.pow(2, 32) - 1 = 4294967295 (index.js:52).",
    "Option description is the source tooltip. Labels are the evaluated source strings (the module builds several labels from range constants, for example \"Brightness (0-10000 nits)\").",
    "Variables, presets and the polling state are not catalogued. Built on @companion-module/base ^1.11.3: options do not support expressions. Manifest version is 0.0.0, package.json version is 2.2.0."
  ]
